{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard","id":1504897,"title":"[Necro] How can I showcase the evil of the Seers Of Throne without going overboard?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-08T20:23:43-08:00","id":1504897,"title":"[Necro] How can I showcase the evil of the Seers Of Throne without going overboard?","content":"In summary, given what I know about real life atrocities committed by powerful people throughout history, it seems to me that portraying the Seers of the Throne in a strictly realistic fashion would require me to narrate scenes involving topics that many players would find excessively upsetting, like child soldiers, forced prostitution, religious persecution, slavery in cellphone factories, and so forth. What options do I have, besides putting all that horror in the background and/or seeking players with different levels of tolerance for such extreme topics?<br /> <br /> My guess is that I can lean closer to the idea of Seers as James Bond-esque villains who &quot;already won&quot; and ran out of ideas, so they just rehash what works for maintaining power ad infinitum. The kind of people who may or may not hate their jobs, but are not allowed to leave lest they become a liability in terms of operational security. But once they come home, they have to spend an hour in subservient prayer to their respective Exarchs, in front of a pyramid-shaped alter, and on their hands and knees. For examples of how Seers want to be seen VS who they truly are, I'm considering using the videos below as references, respectively. I don't get the memes in the second video, I just get Exarchal vibes from it, to be clear. What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/e7gR7EYjcP8\" data-code=\"e7gR7EYjcP8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/e7gR7EYjcP8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YqaxQmjsb2A\" data-code=\"YqaxQmjsb2A\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YqaxQmjsb2A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T20:30:41-08:00","id":1504898,"title":"","content":"Honestly, just go the punch-clock villain route. They're an ass while &quot;on the job&quot;, but if the players meet them on their off hours they're affable and friendly. And genuinely avoids underhanded stuff like <u>Web Weaving</u> some Sympathy off the glass the player was just drinking out of, not that the players need to know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T23:54:58-08:00","id":1504908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard#post1504897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the memes in the second video, I just get Exarchal vibes from it, to be clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woof, that's some real cryptofash stuff there. The representative of the &quot;globalist bankers&quot; controlling the world is pointedly named as &quot;Mr. Rothschild,&quot; Wojaks, the channel's other thumbnails have &quot;you will eat the bugs&quot; and &quot;you'll own nothing and you'll be happy,&quot; &quot;the clown timeline.&quot; These memes exist at a point of intersection between channer culture and Infowars. I'm not blaming you for it, but I don't like having been shown this video. <hr /><br /> You don't have to go hard on the extremes of the banality of evil, nor do you have to showcase it directly. You don't need to personally view the suffering and poverty inflicted to know that a company is using sweatshop labor and that that is bad and hurting people; you don't need to go straight to child soldiers and human trafficking. The corebook has an example Seer of the Throne monologuing internally about how he is funding gentrification projects that will attract commercial business to an area and thereby raise the cost of living and reduce the availability of affordable housing.<br /> <br /> Now I would imagine in the average game, the process of fighting that Seer isn't going to look like a community-building solidarity movement so much as genre action horror where you build sympathy through catspaws to one another building to a confrontation in the Astral Realms while he dons the Profane Urim to weaponize innocent human lives against you, because this is a hobby for entertainment as much as it is an artistic pursuit. If you need moments to make it personal and visceral, you might be better off showcasing the things the Seers are capable of doing individually, to protect themselves and acquire resources for their projects, rather than showcasing the actual long-term projects that subjugate the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Remember also that the Seers of the Throne don't make up the sum total or even the majority of the Exarchs' thrall over the world. A lot of banal evil goes on without their involvement, and they don't have a constant hotline to the will of their masters so much as revelatory fever-visions pointing them in sinister directions. Ultimately, the Seers of the Throne serve <i>themselves</i> before any others, with abasement to the hidden masters as merely a means to sate their selfish ambitions. They are in it because it is an easy way to translate the gift of Awakening into executive credit lines and friends in high places without making dangerous enemies. They prefer to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven. In the absence of clear attention and direction from their Exarch master, pylons are likely to pursue projects that they can justify as pleasing to their Ministry, but which <i>coincidentally</i> harness the Mysteries to garner personal power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T01:43:48-08:00","id":1504915,"title":"","content":"You have the option of putting some horrible stuff in the background, and/or giving the players (and characters) the option to investigate.<br /> <br /> Maybe they decide out of character to just go after the ringleaders (possibly sleepers running the show) or focus on the Pylon and ignore the horrible shit.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they decide to investigate fully and deal with the personal tragedy, horror, etc.<br /> <br /> It depends on the type of game you want to run, and what your players are interested in playing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T02:15:33-08:00","id":1504917,"title":"","content":"There are two additional methods you can use:<br /> <br /> 1) Scale down the evil. You can depict: injustice in civil courts, effects of gentrification, toxic work environments, cronyism in academia... Look for Reddit threads about worst things that happened to average people, and find something your players can handle.<br /> <br /> 2) Scale up the fantasy. Making sure the evil is supernatural in nature allows for greater emotional detachment. replace child soldiers with Myrmidons, prostitution with Hollow ones programmed to enjoy it, slavery with zombies, make Seers tamper with ephemeral realms etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T02:20:35-08:00","id":1504918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504917#post1504917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slavery with zombies</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, recycling isn't evil, it's just good sense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T02:23:52-08:00","id":1504919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard#post1504897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...besides putting all that horror in the background...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that may well be true for Seers themselves. Doing this stuff in-person is not terribly efficient.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd keep in mind that as we're shown, there a lot of ways to oppress the sleepers without doing things that are all that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T03:05:23-08:00","id":1504920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504918#post1504918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, recycling isn't evil, it's just good sense!</div> </div> </div> </div>I must concede that point!<br /> <br /> You have to get extra evil to make that work. Have families forced to sell grandma because they can't afford the next meal, never mind a funeral. Or have debt-slaves for whom death <i>wasn't</i> a way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T03:08:42-08:00","id":1504921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504920#post1504920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or have debt-slaves for whom death <i>wasn't</i> a way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sounds like a good idea for a Psychopomp-centred legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T03:21:38-08:00","id":1504923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504921#post1504921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's sounds like a good idea for a Psychopomp-centred legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeeh... the Bokor already exist tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T06:12:19-08:00","id":1504931,"title":"","content":"I find that Last Week Tonight with John Oliver gives me a lot of insight into all of the many and varied low-key ways in which modern society is constructed to exploit people, and to me all of that feels like exactly the sort of thing Seers of the Throne across the world would latch onto and employ their powers to preserve and perpetuate it.<br /> <br /> I mean, look at the characters in Nameless and Accursed. There's a person who functions as a social chameleon to occupy whatever position might absorb information useful to eir Pylon and the Ministry of Panopticon as a whole, a woman who promotes a scheduling app intended to make people ever more deeply enslave themselves to an automatically-generated schedule, and a guy who is basically a Jordan Peterson stand in.<br /> <br /> You refer to historical atrocities, but those tend to be about making people die. Consider the possibilities inherent to ensuring that people have long full lives that are completely miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T06:18:06-08:00","id":1504932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504918#post1504918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, recycling isn't evil, it's just good sense!</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think of devotees of the Chancellor who see a lot of value in promoting the idea that recycling is actually a lot more useful than it is as a way of keeping people ever more invested in systems of consuming scarce resources to create universally employed products with brief shelf lives and a very long time to exist is non-degradable waste. Certainly, the extent to which plastic pervades in modern society and consumer goods seems like the sort of thing that would evince the principles of that Exarch.<br /> <br /> Oh, I'm also now remembering Good Omens. Crowley's frustration with his superiors that devote themselves to something like the corruption of a single righteous priest and just cannot fathom the value of his projects such as ensuring that road systems are more inefficient in a way that makes commuting unnecessarily frustrating, leading to legions of office workers who will then take out their anger on secretaries and other subordinates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T13:40:39-08:00","id":1504971,"title":"","content":"You could run the Seers of Mammon as aiming to become akin to Marshall, Carter &amp; Dark, I think <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bA1YkqRcFxE\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a> presents their train of thought and goal very nicely. Everything had a price, nothing has value, everything can be purchased. The deals might be fair, but the price will not be, you always leave behind more than you get. But still, you may get rotes, rare Grimoires, rare reference materials, exotic components and even souls, provided you are willing to pay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T17:36:57-08:00","id":1504988,"title":"","content":"I also think that something inherent to the pyramidal structure of the Seers is that the majority of them are engaged in work that is primarily about building their capital. Acts of infiltration, subversion, deal making. The busywork of making large numbers of influential people beholden, which then gets transmitted from the person who made the deal up to the level of a superior who employs that leverage on the strategic level, coordinated with numerous other operations, in order to apply the pressure that cultivates and nurtures the oppressive systems that the Seers are concerned with.<br /> <br /> The Seer that you're most likely to meet if you're not part of a cabal that is concerned with dedicated opposition to them isn't kicking puppies, they're doing things like divining which member of an advertising firm has vulnerabilities, whether those be in things such as greed, being beholden to others, or a hurt that they want relieved, and applying powers to the purpose of covertly addressing those things after having established a quid pro quo with the person, that one day (and that day will definitely come) the Seer will come to them seeking a favour. That advertising executive will be directed as part of an operation coordinated with the actions of several other people, and now the incidence of people consuming large quantities of soft drinks has gone up, creating knock on effects in public healthcare and the pharmaceutical industry and a lot of public commentators hemming and hawing over obesity epidemics and greater incidences of people being derided over their physical appearance.<br /> <br /> The thing is, most Seers don't really see the big picture. If you're a soldier of the Iron Pyramid, you get told to go somewhere and carry out some objective without ever really knowing what it's meant to accomplish. If you're the head of your Pylon, you might have the smarts to know what your general objective for building influence or applying pressure might be in service of, and bringing other Pylons under your umbrella to exert greater and greater control over implementing these procedures is part of how you rise in status... but often you're only slightly less in the dark.<br /> <br /> In either case, on your off hours you live like somebody who has at least a six figure annual salary without putting in quite that amount of work or career building, as well as the general thrill of exerting power over the lives of other people, so you're satisfied.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle cabal dedicated in warfare probably needs to look past these peons. Killing a decent number of them off might slow down the flow of power to the top of the tetrarchy, but it's easily noticed by some very powerful mages, who are liable to close ranks, observe their attackers, and apply a lot of their banked power to destroy them. It's ultimately more effective to spend your time tracing the sequences of reporting to superiors, mapping out the local pyramid, identifying the people at the higher levels. Kill off somebody in the middle, and you create some chaos for a while as everybody below them scrambles to fill the vacancy. Find a person at the top (and determine that they aren't an archmage), and if you can get to them you can do some real damage when the lower ranks stop receiving their orders and all of that power held in reserve becomes inaccessible, the equivalent of a bank account that nobody has the access code to anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T20:36:11-08:00","id":1505080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504908#post1504908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woof, that's some real cryptofash stuff there. The representative of the &quot;globalist bankers&quot; controlling the world is pointedly named as &quot;Mr. Rothschild,&quot; Wojaks, the channel's other thumbnails have &quot;you will eat the bugs&quot; and &quot;you'll own nothing and you'll be happy,&quot; &quot;the clown timeline.&quot; These memes exist at a point of intersection between channer culture and Infowars. I'm not blaming you for it, but I don't like having been shown this video.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>(Watches the channel's other videos)</i><br /> <br /> Huh. Unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Have these videos as substitutes, then, if that is a point of contention.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KICArqH2jNU\" data-code=\"KICArqH2jNU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KICArqH2jNU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7sotIsQ4-Gg\" data-code=\"7sotIsQ4-Gg\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7sotIsQ4-Gg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I actually had an idea for a similar scene that I never got to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine a Praetorian at the end of his rope and running out of personal usefulness to his Ministry, and showing clear willingness to abandon the Iron Pyramid. The General might become so fed up with this Seer's failures and imminent desertion that he sends an Ochema just to make a very brutal example of him. And it's not even especially gory, it's more humiliating. I am imagining that the Ochema rips the Seer's badge of authority from his uniform and crushes it, then takes one look at the Seer and vaporizes him with the Thunderbolt spell. The Seer's miserable Myrmidon bodyguard is terrified out of his mind, and the Ochema says the following to the Myrmidon before returning to the Supernal: &quot;tell the rest of his Pylon to work harder, <u><b>or else</b></u>.&quot; It's important to me that Seers are depicted as ultimately disposable to their masters, and also depicted as not really being in control of their own lives. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1504908#post1504908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to go hard on the extremes of the banality of evil, nor do you have to showcase it directly. You don't need to personally view the suffering and poverty inflicted to know that a company is using sweatshop labor and that that is bad and hurting people; you don't need to go straight to child soldiers and human trafficking. The corebook has an example Seer of the Throne monologuing internally about how he is funding gentrification projects that will attract commercial business to an area and thereby raise the cost of living and reduce the availability of affordable housing.<br /> <br /> Now I would imagine in the average game, the process of fighting that Seer isn't going to look like a community-building solidarity movement so much as genre action horror where you build sympathy through catspaws to one another building to a confrontation in the Astral Realms while he dons the Profane Urim to weaponize innocent human lives against you, because this is a hobby for entertainment as much as it is an artistic pursuit. If you need moments to make it personal and visceral, you might be better off showcasing the things the Seers are capable of doing individually, to protect themselves and acquire resources for their projects, rather than showcasing the actual long-term projects that subjugate the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Remember also that the Seers of the Throne don't make up the sum total or even the majority of the Exarchs' thrall over the world. A lot of banal evil goes on without their involvement, and they don't have a constant hotline to the will of their masters so much as revelatory fever-visions pointing them in sinister directions. Ultimately, the Seers of the Throne serve <i>themselves</i> before any others, with abasement to the hidden masters as merely a means to sate their selfish ambitions. They are in it because it is an easy way to translate the gift of Awakening into executive credit lines and friends in high places without making dangerous enemies. They prefer to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven. In the absence of clear attention and direction from their Exarch master, pylons are likely to pursue projects that they can justify as pleasing to their Ministry, but which <i>coincidentally</i> harness the Mysteries to garner personal power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, these are good points, especially when it comes to genre conventions and the indirect, interpretive &quot;communication&quot; between Seers and Exarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T20:40:01-08:00","id":1505082,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> Thanks to you folks as well, your feedback has really opened my eyes and removed some mental roadblocks that made it significantly hard for me to conceptualize what Seers actually DO in a professional-tyrant sense. I'm writing all of this feedback down on a Word file for my Mage folder, and will use it to expand and adjust some vague concepts for Seer NPCs I have stored away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T06:26:55-08:00","id":1505110,"title":"","content":"A thing worth keeping in mind is that the Seers of the Throne often take actions that might seem to make no sense. If the commands from their superiors in Ministry and tetrarchy are often obscure*, those from the Exarchs are truly esoteric.<br /> <br /> The direct dream commands are one thing; they might be conveyed largely in terms of image rather than word, but they're supposed to be understandable enough. Just think about how where they're coming from can mean one's actions are very much part of a strategy of three-dimensional chess, a move being directed from a vantage point of space and time that no human can comprehend.<br /> <br /> But then there's the fact that Seers believe the Exarchs' mastery of the world pervade it with signs and omens that reveal their will, to be determined with mortal divinations. These bear out results often enough to not be completely off the mark, but how are Seers to tell the false positive from the real ones? Better to just do it all and feel secure in the knowledge that <i>some</i> of them are on target.<br /> <br /> So there are Seers of the Throne who are literally taking action because their horoscopes said so.<br /> <br /> That should give a lot of latitude in what sorts of actions one portrays Seers of the Throne as taking on the daily. It can be a bit of a balancing act, as one probably doesn't want to make them totally farcical, but... don't make them <i>not</i> farcical. There is supposed to be something a bit absurd about being in the Iron Pyramid.<br /> <br /> Former developer Dave Brookshaw literally wrote the book on Seers of the Throne**, and in the actual play that put him on the map his players dealt with one troublesome Seer by mind controlling a guy on a drug trip into telling him to walk into a trap.<br /> <br /> * Which can include being assigned tasks that are literally pointless, for reasons including &quot;test their loyalty&quot;, &quot;determine their thresholds&quot; and &quot;waste their time&quot;.<br /> ** Along with several others, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T14:58:21-07:00","id":1505195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1505110#post1505110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is supposed to be something a bit absurd about being in the Iron Pyramid.<br /> <br /> Former developer Dave Brookshaw literally wrote the book on Seers of the Throne**, and in the actual play that put him on the map his players dealt with one troublesome Seer by mind controlling a guy on a drug trip into telling him to walk into a trap.<br /> <br /> ** Along with several others, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, he clearly stated in Soul Cage, that in his Opinion, (at the time not a main Mage writer) the World was a prison made by the Exarchs, and the Seers might think they are the prison guards, but they are actually prison snitches.<br /> <br /> Just as much trapped in the Soul Cage as everyone else, but also working to reinforce the bars...yeah, Seers not painted particularly sympathicly anywhere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T15:41:13-07:00","id":1505199,"title":"","content":"Not to say there isn't room to make them sympathetic, at least the low-level mooks. Some may have joined the Seers because they didn't know there was an alternative, some might have the heads mans axe hanging over their loved ones, etc. <br /> <br /> Once you reach Status 3 or so though -and absolutely if you're a Minister or Tetrarch- the margin for being misunderstood borders on nil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T16:09:56-07:00","id":1505203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1505199#post1505199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say there isn't room to make them sympathetic, at least the low-level mooks. Some may have joined the Seers because they didn't know there was an alternative, some might have the heads mans axe hanging over their loved ones, etc.<br /> <br /> Once you reach Status 3 or so though -and absolutely if you're a Minister or Tetrarch- the margin for being misunderstood borders on nil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it's been mentioned, but if I passed on a chance to refer to the Seers of the Throne as the Tyranny of the Defeated, I'll have missed something, so I'm going to mildly disagree about even high end Seers being unsympathetic.<br /> <br /> The big thing to the Seers, whether they be punch-clock metaphysician or priest of the asshole tyrants, is that all of them gave up at some point on something at some point. Maybe it's just that trying to fathom the unfathomable just gets to be too much, maybe it's because the Lie seems too engrained into reality, maybe it's because you lose the ability to see the way things can be played beyond the rigged game, but there's this point where every Seer just can't pay or fight or believe in <i>something</i> anymore, and submission to the system of the Exarchs becomes the only major viable way forward to their eyes.<br /> <br /> I think, particularly as you get older, it becomes easy, at time, to just have a crisis of faith-about the goodness of people, about the ability to change systems and ideas, about the ability to do-something, <i>anything, <u>just that one thing that will make the one difference</u></i>-no matter how much more aware and personally powerful we get. The world just always find new and awful ways to punch down. Seers are born from these sorts of crises-and metaphysical fuckery asides, they carry it with them.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's a Seer alive, from the lowliest grunt to the nearly Ascendant archmage, who you couldn't find the right sort of question, the right sort of What If or Unless that wouldn't make them stop and ponder what could have been, who they might've been if they just held faith a little longer. They might not have reason to believe that that version of themselves ever had any power, had any hope-but I think there's still a pause in each of them, that way in which the Defeat they accept never really stops hurting even if it's a numbing sort of pain. Some of them might not even realize that that's the case, but they could. Only the Ascendant get to escape it<br /> <br /> And in it's that defeat, whatever it's form, that, for however hateful and awful the Tyranny of the Defeated can be, that I think you'll always find a bit of humanity. It may be the very reason you might owe them death rather than redemption, but it's in that weakness that everyone is still like unto each other. I think every mage eventually runs into that problem, and I think every mage has that quiet issue where, no matter how powerful they are, they just aren't always strong enough to handle the Fallen World, and see how the Seers took what was, for as awful as it is, a very human way out.<br /> <br /> You can't always win. What seperates the Pentacle from the Seers is the choice of the ideal against it's reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T16:28:48-07:00","id":1505205,"title":"","content":"Sure, but there's a difference between having a sympathetic backstory and being sympathetic in the now.<br /> <br /> Being able to trace the trajectory that leads someone to become the archbishop of the Church of War Crimes can be absolutely heartbreaking, but doesn't necessarily make them any less culpable for what they've done. Nor does it change the fact that they've bought so far into this system that they now order the atrocities committed rather than conducting them themselves.<br /> <br /> It's certainly <i>possible</i> to have them be sympathetic, tired old men and women who've been doing what they have to to survive and regretting every choice, but I somehow doubt you can reach that high in the service of the Exarch and still retain your morals. Either you break under the strain, you give in, or you get culled for insufficient dedication by your superiors or subordinates. <br /> <br /> ... Come to think of it, did Imperial Mysteries ever mention ex-Seer Archmages who <i>didn't</i> join the Tetrach Entente?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T17:12:43-07:00","id":1505212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1505205#post1505205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but there's a difference between having a sympathetic backstory and being sympathetic in the now.<br /> <br /> Being able to trace the trajectory that leads someone to become the archbishop of the Church of War Crimes can be absolutely heartbreaking, but doesn't necessarily make them any less culpable for what they've done. Nor does it change the fact that they've bought so far into this system that they now order the atrocities committed rather than conducting them themselves.<br /> <br /> It's certainly <i>possible</i> to have them be sympathetic, tired old men and women who've been doing what they have to to survive and regretting every choice, but I somehow doubt you can reach that high in the service of the Exarch and still retain your morals. Either you break under the strain, you give in, or you get culled for insufficient dedication by your superiors or subordinates.<br /> <br /> ... Come to think of it, did Imperial Mysteries ever mention ex-Seer Archmages who <i>didn't</i> join the Tetrach Entente?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, I agree, and I even made that point when I said &quot;that might be the reason you owe them death rather than redemption.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T17:56:07-07:00","id":1505213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504897-necro-how-can-i-showcase-the-evil-of-the-seers-of-throne-without-going-overboard?p=1505203#post1505203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure it's been mentioned, but if I passed on a chance to refer to the Seers of the Throne as the Tyranny of the Defeated, I'll have missed something, so I'm going to mildly disagree about even high end Seers being unsympathetic.<br /> <br /> The big thing to the Seers, whether they be punch-clock metaphysician or priest of the asshole tyrants, is that all of them gave up at some point on something at some point. Maybe it's just that trying to fathom the unfathomable just gets to be too much, maybe it's because the Lie seems too engrained into reality, maybe it's because you lose the ability to see the way things can be played beyond the rigged game, but there's this point where every Seer just can't pay or fight or believe in <i>something</i> anymore, and submission to the system of the Exarchs becomes the only major viable way forward to their eyes.<br /> <br /> I think, particularly as you get older, it becomes easy, at time, to just have a crisis of faith-about the goodness of people, about the ability to change systems and ideas, about the ability to do-something, <i>anything, <u>just that one thing that will make the one difference</u></i>-no matter how much more aware and personally powerful we get. The world just always find new and awful ways to punch down. Seers are born from these sorts of crises-and metaphysical fuckery asides, they carry it with them.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's a Seer alive, from the lowliest grunt to the nearly Ascendant archmage, who you couldn't find the right sort of question, the right sort of What If or Unless that wouldn't make them stop and ponder what could have been, who they might've been if they just held faith a little longer. They might not have reason to believe that that version of themselves ever had any power, had any hope-but I think there's still a pause in each of them, that way in which the Defeat they accept never really stops hurting even if it's a numbing sort of pain. Some of them might not even realize that that's the case, but they could. Only the Ascendant get to escape it<br /> <br /> And in it's that defeat, whatever it's form, that, for however hateful and awful the Tyranny of the Defeated can be, that I think you'll always find a bit of humanity. It may be the very reason you might owe them death rather than redemption, but it's in that weakness that everyone is still like unto each other. I think every mage eventually runs into that problem, and I think every mage has that quiet issue where, no matter how powerful they are, they just aren't always strong enough to handle the Fallen World, and see how the Seers took what was, for as awful as it is, a very human way out.<br /> <br /> You can't always win. What seperates the Pentacle from the Seers is the choice of the ideal against it's reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reminded of a Praetorian of mine who was literally born into servitude of his Ministry, and as an in vitro human as well. He was trained in warfare by robots, experimented on with pseudo-scientific and Left-Handed methods, and generally tortured in body, mind and soul soon after his artificial birth to test out a theory related to an Obsession of a higher-ranked Praetorian, which I based on a sidebar of flavor text from Nobilis 3ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you lock a human alone in a room for long enough\u2014past the point of anger, past the point of despair, past the point where they can no longer talk or think coherently \u2014 they begin inventing new methods of war. They begin to create tools and strategies of battle that the world has never seen before. It takes a skilled psychologist to dredge meaning from their mumbles and gibbering, from the sketches their fingernails make against the floor.<br /> <br /> That is the only secret; that is what makes the great nations great, and makes lesser nations fall. Someone locked in a room, in the dark, without sanitation or company, until their mind breaks; someone to read their heart, and tell the world what transpires there.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And yet, he was innocent in the sense that an ichneumon wasp, cancerous organ or nuclear warhead is innocent. And in fact, he was the only Seer in that Chronicle to willingly leave behind the Iron Pyramid and join the Adamantine Arrow. And he didn't do it by looking backward to think of <u><i>What Could Have Been</i></u>, his immense curiosity and dedication paved the way for him to notice that, quite simply, he had suffered something arguably worse than imprisonment and torture: everything he had been told about humanity by his &quot;friends&quot; was part of the Lie. Part of the reason he decided to determine his own destiny is that he was capable of using his superlative intellect and focus to notice <u><i>What Might Ye Be.</i></u><br /> <br /> The future he saw for the Fallen World under the reign of the Praetorians was so... so pointless to him, so samey, so unimaginative that he realized his talents were wasted on serving The General. On that night, Noose stayed up until 4 AM doing nice things for himself for the first time in his life, because nobody else did that for him, like eating ice cream, watching life-affirming children's cartoons, and going to bed normally instead of literally shooting himself in the foot to avoid sleeping and thus having nightmares about war. When he dreamed that night, he saw a mystical omen similar to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tank_Man\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a certain historical episode</b></a> and the first thing he did in the following morning was destroy his Sanctum where he developed machines and strategies for war, and went on a quest of rebirth worthy of a Moros whose conception of the Truth had been fundamentally changed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T18:17:23-07:00","id":1505216,"title":"","content":"While I certainly assume that most people who join the Seers weren't exactly informed of alternatives, at this point I think that reality bears out that there are quite enough people who really are just terrible or insufficiently motivated to challenge terrible systems in which they find themselves, and that pretty much anybody with a rank higher than the bottom is investing themselves in it. I think a sense of fatalism is more often ritualistic than it is some overwhelming rational argument they make to justify themselves.<br /> <br /> I think that where what a lot of Seers do induces them with a lot of stress, this is less of a moral anguish than it is just that they're actions that create intense experiences within the brain, based in how it's wired to react to environmental factors.<br /> <br /> Going by object example, I'd imagine that most Seers who don't cope with that stress with addictions do so with abuse, centering themselves with petty exertions of power.<br /> <br /> More pitiful than pitiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T23:47:55-07:00","id":1552630,"title":"","content":"Never thought I'd see the Bogdanoff twins over here of all places...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}